**Defects in `a877330` (incremental.py):**

1. **`filter_excluded` mutable default argument — major.** `excluded=[]` (incremental.py:10) is created once at def time; every call without an explicit list appends into the same shared list. A second call returns the first call's exclusions plus its own — cross-call state corruption.

2. **`copy_many` reports failed copies as done — major.** `synccli.copy_file` swallows `OSError` internally (`pass`, synccli.py:68-69), so a failed copy never raises; the `try/except` in incremental.py:22-26 never fires and `dst` is appended to `done` anyway. The return value ("dst paths done", i.e. successfully copied) is false for unreadable sources. If the caller updates the manifest from `done` (the obvious use), those files are recorded as synced but were never copied, and subsequent incremental syncs skip them — silent data loss.

3. **`merge_manifest` keeps stale state when mtime goes backward — minor.** incremental.py:38 adopts a new state only if `old[rel]["mtime"] <= state["mtime"]`. A genuine content change with an older mtime (rollback/restore, clock skew) is dropped from the merged manifest, so the manifest misrepresents the destination. (Partly self-healing because `changed_files` compares full state, but the merged manifest itself is wrong.)

4. **`merge_manifest` `KeyError` on entries lacking `"mtime"` — minor.** `old[rel]["mtime"]` (incremental.py:38) crashes on a legacy/hand-edited/corrupt destination manifest, unlike `changed_files`, which tolerates any state shape.
